ESTABLISHED FACTS (from the manuscript text)
============================================================
Dusty
- Very tall (a head over most people), long reach, street fighter since childhood. Black eyes.
- Mana: a candle flame, orange, with a black haze and a hairline silver edge around his fingers. Never runs out; can hold it all night. Used the glow nightly to warm Rinnie's back.
- Speech: "sir", "ma'am", "please", "I'm sorry". States brutal facts flatly, "like the price of rye" (a recurring comparison).
- Has only just started calling Valia by name. Told no one his parents' story except Valia.
- Knows the saintess lore only from the soup priests.
- Injuries from the Greys fight (cheek, thigh, back) haven't been mentioned since.

Rinnie
- 12. Black hair and eyes, milk-pale lips, bruised under-eyes, bird-boned, cold hands. Must eat slowly or she vomits. Overexertion costs her the next day (or more).
- The blue ribbon was a gift from Dusty at 8.
- Wants to be a Maid (asked). Asks questions constantly; hides her trembling hands (mentioned in Dusty's memory).
- Has claimed Valia as Dusty's minder via a promise.

Valia
- Shorter than Dusty; pink waist-length braid; light blue wide eyes; pointed ears; blushes to the tips.
- On-page outfit: green wool cloak (thinned at the elbows), high-necked woolen blouse, baggy traveling pants, heeled brown boots. Her father's brown robe is only seen folded on her bed.
- Research: mana plus sound, 40 years. Lab in the EAST WING, with copper wire on iron posts. Eats alone at the end seat by the window. Faculty say "we'll look into it."
- Carries clutter in nested pockets. Has done Way Station travel 30-40 times.
- Grief tell shown once (at "Ever since—"). Hasn't said her father's name on the page.

Maids
- Silent movement, teleport-fast repositioning. The Guard fears them; inns defer to them.
- Maxim: "Beauty, Elegance, and Dignity above all else."
- Origin hint: they served "a monster" who died, then chose the academy.
- One Maid is assigned to Valia's lab at a time (implied: "Maids trading places in her lab").
- Open "permission" thread (see below).

Guards
- Holt: big, heavy jaw, spear-first, knows where Valia's papers are. Pell: thin mouth, contemptuous, snorts at questions. Both were dismissed in Aethres; they're terrified of the Maids.

World
- Helvanthor: capital(-ish) city; upper city spires, a cathedral with bells, lower market, the Greys (slum), the Devout Quarter. At war with the north for years. The city guard burns out coughing-sickness streets with people inside.
- The Church runs Way Stations; crystals are grown and cost a fortune. Calvenne is another destination.
- Saintesses exist: young girls, heavily guarded, led by the wrist.
- The academy's 100-mile no-crown zone around the lake. Mythrandis colors are blue with a white tower.
- Three disciplines (healing named as one).
- Travel: Helvanthor to the Duke's town by Way Station, then five days' ride to Aethres. Aethres sits at the mainland end of the bridge.

